<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 90 0 R
/T (1. Scanner Buffer Mismatches: The use of scanner.nextInt\(\) caused the line-feed delimiters to remain in the input buffer, thereby causing trailing string inputs to be overlooked. This problem was solved by standardising the input readings onto scanner.nextLine\(\) and then using Integer.parseInt\(\).  )
/E (1. Scanner Buffer Mismatches: The use of scanner.nextInt\(\) caused the line-feed delimiters to remain in the input buffer, thereby causing trailing string inputs to be overlooked. This problem was solved by standardising the input readings onto scanner.nextLine\(\) and then using Integer.parseInt\(\).  )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 90 0 R
/T (2. Lack of superclass context: In the implementations, casting was needed in order to print the fields of the subclass when referring to the base class. This problem was neatly resolved by directly overriding the display\(\) method through the use of a virtual method call.  )
/E (2. Lack of superclass context: In the implementations, casting was needed in order to print the fields of the subclass when referring to the base class. This problem was neatly resolved by directly overriding the display\(\) method through the use of a virtual method call.  )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
